-- title:
--   Non-regular fibre ring at a crossing point of the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M\ge 5$ with $M\neq 0$ in the `NeZero` sense and $p\nmid M$, and a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, together with a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ generated by the coefficientwise image, under the map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field `x1FunctionFieldC ℚ (M * p)`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A\to L$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with the tower $A\subseteq L\subseteq K$; let $j\in K$ be a nonzero element whose image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ is [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81). Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field. Consider the two-chart model over $A$, the pushout of the two morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusions of the chart algebras attached to $j$ and to $j^{-1}$ into the middle algebra, with its structure morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, and form the pullback along $\mathrm{Spec}\,k\to\mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Let $x$ be a point of this pullback lying on two distinct irreducible components $Z_1\neq Z_2$ of it, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$ and satisfy $\varpi\mapsto 0$ in $k$. Write $z$ for the image of $x$ under the first projection and $\sigma$ for the germ at $z$ of the global section of [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) obtained from $\varpi$ via $A\cong\Gamma(\mathrm{Spec}\,A)$ and pullback along [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.toBase A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L258). The conclusion is that $\sigma$ lies in the maximal ideal of the local ring $\mathcal{O}_{z}$ at $z$, and that the quotient $\mathcal{O}_{z}/(\sigma)$ is not a regular local ring.
--
--   This is the local obstruction step: since the residue field of $A$ is perfect, regularity of the fibre local ring $\mathcal{O}_z/(\varpi)$ would be geometric and would force the local ring of the geometric special fibre at $x$ to be a domain, so $x$ could not lie on two distinct irreducible components. It is used in the analysis of the components of the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.XOneP.fst_mem_chartFinOpen_of_mem_irreducibleComponents_pair_specialFibre_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.fst_mem_chartFinOpen_of_mem_irreducibleComponents_pair_specialFibre_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
